A||||2||jlruiz67||3.4 small block conversion||||1||
Z||000000||jlruiz67||06-17-2000||12:58 PM||||Hello all<P>Has anyone re built a 3.4 camaro small block and then re used all the original fiero parts to finish it off? I need to upgrade my engine very soon (200K and statring to show oil going to the intake)I was thinking on getting a small block 3.4 from a camaro and bore it out for larger pistons and then install a compu cam, change injectors or get a presure regulator, get head work done to my original fiero heads and put it all togeter and go. I'm I dreaming here or is it possible. I know that I will have to drill the new spot for the starter and grind down part of the engine because I have an automatic. If I can do this it will save me a small fortune. No kits and arrownd 200+ HP, Please if you have a opinion let me have it, I can use all the advice you can dish out.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||06-18-2000||01:35 AM||||   JL, not only is it possible, but it's probably the most common swap there is. It is supposed to be the best swap to dollar ratio going for the Fiero. Basicly, you do just as you mentioned in your post, you build your 3.4L block up then put on all of the Fiero 2.8L externals. Of course you'll want to throw for some headers, a nice exhaust system and probably a bored TB and ported plenum. I am doing a similar conversion this coming sping(knock on wood). I am taking a 3.4L short block, stroking and boring, upgraded cam, injectors and adjustable fuel pressure regulator. I am having the heads milled, and upsizing the valves, porting and polishing and matching the intake and exhaust/with sprint headers and hopefully a Borla exhaust sytem with a freeflow cat. There are a few other little things that I may or may not do. My intention is to have a moderately fast and relatively quick Fiero. I like the other conversions, but they are all to pricy for my blood. Besides, a 200+hp 3.4L is plenty for me. It will still rock the "RICER" world a little. Sorry Stimpy, I went there. Metaphoricly speeking, of course. Good luck and keep me..us posted. You should probably do a search of the archives on this subject, you are guaranteed plentifull reading.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
